                "context": "Before publishing a transport-market briefing, check the sales and fleet figures against the cited original report: https://www.iea.org/reports/global-ev-outlook-2024/trends-in-electric-cars . Keep the reporting year and the distinction between sales and stock explicit."
              }
            },
            "output": {
              "type": "json",
              "example": {
                "schemaVersion": "2.0",
                "requestId": "saver-professional-example-20261018-ev-market-check",
                "status": "supported",
                "confidence": 0.99,
                "explanation": "The claim is supported by the cited IEA Global EV Outlook 2024 page. The report says almost 14 million new electric cars were registered globally in 2023 and that this brought the total number of electric cars on roads to 40 million. In the next sentence, it states that electric cars accounted for around 18% of all cars sold in 2023. Because the 18% is explicitly described as a share of cars sold in 2023, while the 40 million figure is described as the total number on the roads, the claim correctly distinguishes sales share from stock/fleet share.",
