                    "id": "e1",
                    "text": "The IEA Global EV Outlook 2024 page says: 'Almost 14 million new electric cars were registered globally in 2023, bringing their total number on the roads to 40 million.' This supports the claim's 2023 global electric-car stock figure and identifies it as cars on the road.",
                    "relation": "supports",
                    "sourceIds": [
                      "s1"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "e2",
                    "text": "The same IEA page says: 'Electric cars accounted for around 18% of all cars sold in 2023, up from 14% in 2022...' This supports the claim's 18% figure and shows it is a sales share for new cars sold in 2023, not the share of all cars already on the road.",
                    "relation": "supports",
                    "sourceIds": [
                      "s1"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "e3",
                    "text": "The IEA page labels the relevant section 'Electric car sales' and includes a chart note stating that BEV and PHEV figures include passenger cars only, providing context for the scope of the sales and stock figures.",
                    "relation": "context",
                    "sourceIds": [
                      "s1"
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "sources": [
                  {
                    "id": "s1",
                    "title": "iea.org",
                    "url": "https://www.iea.org/reports/global-ev-outlook-2024/trends-in-electric-cars"
